{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1337627-esoterica","id":1337627,"title":"Esoterica","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-09-24T06:55:06-07:00","id":1337627,"title":"Esoterica","content":"What's the general ST take on the Esoterica Skill and its application of counting 10s twice for Arete Rolls?<br /> <br /> The description seems to imply it is granted for an entire practice which seems much to broad to me. I was thinking of refining it to a specific focus and the mysteries of such.<br /> <br /> Thoughs?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-24T14:14:47-07:00","id":1337701,"title":"","content":"As written, Esoterica gives you double 10s on Skill rolls, not Arete rolls (unless I missed something in HDYDT). So Esoterica basically has a side bonus of providing you a floating specialty you can apply as long as the esoteric practice would apply. You can get double 10s on a Medicine roll when using herbal medicines if your have Esoterica in Herbology, etc.<br /> <br /> This interacts with Arete as per the standard rules for Abilities doing so.<br /> <br /> The description also references Instruments not Practices when it refers back to Focus. But there really isn't a big deal here. Some Practices are going to be able to cluster Instruments around a small set of Abilities naturally, so Esoterica boosting those Abilities isn't that big of a deal.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-24T15:10:00-07:00","id":1337716,"title":"","content":"As Heavy Arms said it probably isn't really big of a deal. If your Esoterica is based around Alchemy and someone plays an Alchemist, they are already kinda limiting what they are doing already.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25315-jihelu","name":"Jihelu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-24T17:30:44-07:00","id":1337734,"title":"","content":"The skill description says it applies to &quot;mundane and magick-casting rolls that employ the practice&quot;. If that isn't Arete then I'm really misreading it.<br /> <br /> As far being limiting I would say far from it. Yoga and Voodoo are to practices specifically listed as specialties. Each of those, as well as alchemy, can easily fulfill all of many a Mage's needs for casting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-24T18:35:13-07:00","id":1337747,"title":"","content":"Gah, why is that burried in that paragraph.<br /> <br /> Though it's important to quote the whole sentence here, &quot;Say, for example, your character has four dots in Esoterica, with a specialty in Herbalism; if he gets some time to study yoga, he can spend four experience points and then add a specialty in Yoga to that Knowledge\u2026 after which time he can use yoga as a focus tool (assuming that it fits his magickal paradigm), and count 10s as two successes on mundane or magick-casting rolls that employ that practice.&quot;<br /> <br /> So the important bit is the phrase, &quot;...after which time he can use yoga as a focus tool ...&quot; this only makes sense to me as requiring the yoga to be expressed via Instruments/Tools, rather than Practices to gain the benefit.<br /> <br /> But yes, this would mean that you'd get to double 10s if Esoterica would apply to your magic in this fashion. I would probably be more likely to insist on some of the optional stuff to tamp down on abilities and magic working in synergy if you're worried about this getting too potent.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-24T18:44:09-07:00","id":1337748,"title":"","content":"Oh I'm totally for it only applying to &quot;tools&quot; and not an entire practice. That's why I wondered how others played it.<br /> <br /> Really the biggest issue I had was in respect to Voodoo as it is an on again - off again popular paradigm with our group and it's hard to separate it as a tool only.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-25T15:01:11-07:00","id":1337858,"title":"","content":"My PCs tend to have a dot or more in Esoterica. Tarot, Symbolism, Runes, Herbalism etc.<br /> <br /> If they're prepared to make a ritual of what they're doing, and it's all justified, they can reduce the difficulty of an Arete roll as per the M20 rules. So Jayden could use his Tarot ability (rolling Perception + Esoterica perhaps) before trying to read someone's mind with Mind.<br /> <br /> I haven't run into any problems with this, but it does occur to me that if the situation isn't time-pressured it's ALWAYS better to do an ability preparation roll if you can. If you're going to sing to do magick, then do a Charisma + Art (Singing) roll first. If you're going to rig up a hypertech device to blow something up, it's better to do that Intelligence + Hypertech roll. I suppose I could just make this sort of standard, to represent how the actual skill is the foundation of someone's practice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-25T16:29:15-07:00","id":1337870,"title":"","content":"The only slight downside of using an ability to make your magick easier is you can't spend Willpower on the roll, so if the DC is super low anyway it may be better to get the extra success.<br /> <br /> Maybe.<br /> <br /> I'm sure there is math that proves me wrong tho. If you can already get an easy -3 to your roll (IE: Quintessence/Node nearby/Other stuff) it's better to not do the ability lowering.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25315-jihelu","name":"Jihelu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-25T16:59:04-07:00","id":1337879,"title":"","content":"According to the skill description there is no need to make an Esoterica skill roll before working the effect. If you have the specialty for the practice it grants double 10s on the Arete roll<br /> <br /> Honestly I think the main problem is that the skill is badly worded. Like mentioned earlier if it only applys the bonus to a specific tool then there isn't really much of an issue. It's when its applied to an entire practice that it becomes OP. 1 skill specialty could end up giving the equivalent of a specialty in all spheres for all effects cast by the Mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-25T22:14:05-07:00","id":1337931,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I think the Esoterica entry is just weirdly worded; The way I read the 'magick-casting rolls' part, it essentially refers to Esoterica (given it's a candidate of the Well-Skilled-Craftsman rule) being a good way to get the double-10's when using the M20 rule of using an ability to reduce the Arete difficulty. That's the 'magick-casting' part of it. After all, depending on the instrument in question, there are even some practices where you *have* to roll the ability in order to do the Arete roll.<br /> <br /> You can already get double-10's on Arete rolls themselves starting with Sphere Ratings of 4+ (an often overlooked thing in M20) by courtesy of the Specialty rules. Granted, those only apply to a specific kind of effect more than a specific practice, but that's also what makes more sense for Arete rolls themselves.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Shere Specialties</b><br /> Each of the following entries also features a selection of<br /> specialties. You can choose a Sphere specialty when your mage<br /> accumulates four dots in that Sphere. As with the specialties<br /> granted to Attributes and Abilities, a Sphere specialty allows<br /> you to count each 10 you roll as two successes, not just one.<br /> <i>(For details, see Chapter Six, p. 274.)</i><br /> At four dots, a player gets to choose one specialty, based<br /> upon the things the mage does most often with the Sphere<br /> in question. At the Storyteller\u2019s discretion, additional specialties<br /> can be purchased for four experience points each, assuming<br /> that the character has spent time and effort training herself in that<br /> specialty. You can\u2019t suddenly specialize in Shapeshifting, after<br /> all, if your character hasn\u2019t spent lots of time learning how to<br /> change her shape. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 09-26-2019, 01:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-25T22:41:48-07:00","id":1337932,"title":"","content":"That's certainly how I'd probably run it, but the phrasing of the Skill is vague enough that I can't argue against the other way based on the text itself.<br /> <br /> I think how big a deal it is depends a lot of how many of the optional rules you use. Because really, the way Abilities enhancing Magick works is already more potent than double 10s on Arete would be in terms of what you'd want to get use out of.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}